 "note": "L is subtype M6A/M6B (Table 3, M column); S is subtype M6A (Table 4, M6A column). The orbit (0,0,0,0) is the shared rotation centre, filling 1 on both sides, so the graph has 374 + 136 - 1 = 509 vertices and 2442 edges. Orbit labels are Parts's canonical representatives (a,b,c,d) of the point (a + b*sqrt33 + i(c*sqrt3 + d*sqrt11))/12. A filling below the orbit size means the orbit is PARTIAL and which members are taken is NOT in the table -- section 6 says unfilled orbits 'usually include exactly half or a quarter', i.e. whole orbits of an index-2 or index-4 subgroup. Vertex lists are published at reference [11]: Polymath16 thread 15 comment 24942, and the Dropbox folder JP/Large.",
